hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3024","**\nNarrated to us ʿAlī ibn Khashram: ʿĪsā informed us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who narrated to me Mūsā ibn ʿUqbah, on the authority of Nāfiʿ, that Ibn ʿUmar (RA) informed him:\n\n*\The Prophet (ﷺ) shaved his head during the Farewell Pilgrimage.\""*\n\nHe (Ibn ʿUmar) said: At that time"","" people would shave their heads during Hajj"","" then perform ʿUmrah at Minā. The Prophet (ﷺ) said: *\""What is this man shaving for?\""* So we would say to one of them: *\""Pass the razor over your head.\""*"""""
